# S5-07 fault-time frame-chain schema-v3 diagnostic pair, 2026-11-15

Purpose: resolve the caller chain at the variably observed CPL0 page fault in
`rep_movs_alternative+0x11`. These are two independent counted single runs,
not an automatic N=2 series. No comparator was run; this evidence does not
accept S5-07.

## Source, host, binary and inputs

- Worktree/branch: `codex`, source commit
  `f59d06d00e9c14eb703ff86c3c4e31c2fb2adcbe`, clean before the runs.
- Host: Darwin arm64. Release `od-runner` SHA-256:
  `43a44a98219b49fd78bf2829a00892277423d5cd8a030ee3e05a3b52a48941a0`.
- Kernel SHA-256:
  `9f55ef7253055a9cf68f8a04323c93dead2fca617386d842fbde9ca7b178b27e`.
- Initramfs SHA-256:
  `ee9183a4eded3c16a8c6a7a81c6d5bb79be8bb023f793f7cd61694ea2bd3e588`.
- ACPI blob SHA-256:
  `b1ba6078a4d9bc7a8d224980713d8242e4a708743ce4f56093b00a07c631ffaf`;
  manifest hash `2bd690ae0817705b1b128675f9628dd7212fee74ab97c88da3599a1ae8e398f2`.
- Matching `vmlinux-debug-7.0.0-38-generic` SHA-256:
  `7e460f048c3de0f8ee85fd326f2f65d95a6ee448e57b6f5333e2be79b5be9d1f`.
- Both runs used 128 MiB, counted `stage4a`, release, budget
