  `budget_exhausted`. Inputs and run flags match the preceding schema-v2
  diagnostic pair; only nonce and output directory changed.

## Results

Both reports say `status=loaded`, `acceptance=counted`, `guest_started=true`,
and reached `retired=2,999,999,998` with the exact nonce. Both sidecars are
schema v3 and have zero omitted #PF records.

| Run | Nonce | #PF | RDTSC | IRQ0 edges / delivered | Quanta | Virtual ns | CPL3 retired |
|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| `k` | `od5fchain20261115k` | 34 | 34,450,164 | 34,811 / 34,816 | 34,575,842 | 37,468,905,987 | 906 |
| `l` | `od5fchain20261115l` | 33 | 34,446,427 | 34,807 / 34,812 | 34,572,344 | 37,464,465,341 | 906 |

Both sidecars retained the same 22 distinct RDTSC sites. Of the total delta
of 3,737 reads, 3,647 are at `0xffffffff8271b34d` (`delay_tsc+0x4d`); the
other nine changed sites account for the remaining 90 reads. This localizes
the count variation to the delay loop but does not explain why the guest
executes a different number of iterations.

The first 30 fault signatures match. Run `k` has one extra event at index 30;
after aligning past it, all later signatures match run `l`:

| Field | Run `k`, event 30 |
|---|---|
| RIP / symbol | `0xffffffff8271a9c1`, `rep_movs_alternative+0x11` |
| Instruction | byte store `MOVB AL,(RDI)` |
| Access / CPL / error | Write / 0 / `0x00000002` |
| CR2 = RDI | `0x7ffc63ea4399` |
| CR3 | `0x648a000` |
| RSP / RBP | `0xffffc9000000fc80` / `0xffffc9000000fc88` |
| RCX / RSI | `0x7` / `0xffffffff82fdeb8f` |
| Captured frames / end | 10 / `UnalignedFramePointer` |

The following table lists the frame-pointer slot and its saved return address.
GNU `addr2line` 2.47, using the matching debug ELF above, resolved these
addresses:

| Frame pointer | Return address | Resolved function + offset |
|---|---|---|
| `0xffffc9000000fc88` | `0xffffffff81999bd9` | `create_elf_tables+0x99` |
| `0xffffc9000000fd10` | `0xffffffff8199c32c` | `load_elf_binary+0xb0c` |
| `0xffffc9000000fdd8` | `0xffffffff818f1cbc` | `search_binary_handler` inlined in `exec_binprm+0x13c` |
| `0xffffc9000000fe38` | `0xffffffff818f2020` | `bprm_execve.part.0+0x160` |
| `0xffffc9000000fe70` | `0xffffffff818f210a` | `bprm_execve+0x4a` |
| `0xffffc9000000fe90` | `0xffffffff818f4682` | `kernel_execve+0x112` |
| `0xffffc9000000fec8` | `0xffffffff812002b3` | `run_init_process+0xf3` |
| `0xffffc9000000fee8` | `0xffffffff8272caa5` | `kernel_init+0xb5` |
| `0xffffc9000000ff00` | `0xffffffff813b2525` | `ret_from_fork+0x195` |
| `0xffffc9000000ff38` | `0xffffffff81346aca` | `ret_from_fork_asm+0x1a` |

Run `l` has no corresponding event: its event 30 is the CPL3 fetch fault at
`RIP=CR2=0x4000b0` with null RBP, and its sidecar records
`frame_chain_end=NullFramePointer`. Thus the chain in `k` localizes that extra
fault to a byte store while Linux is executing the ELF loading / initial stack
setup path rooted at `create_elf_tables`. Together with `RCX=7` and RSI's
previously verified `x86_64\0` bytes, this supports a startup-stack string-copy
interpretation. It does not prove the exact copy purpose or why the page fault
is absent in run `l`; no pre/post PTE state was captured. The termination at
`UnalignedFramePointer` also means the trace is bounded evidence, not a complete
unwind.

The counts vary between these independent runs: one delivered #PF, 3,737
RDTSC reads, four IRQ0 edges / deliveries, and 3,498 quanta. No comparator ran,
no differences are classified benign, and no normalization changed. The
frame-chain reader is opt-in; its wall-time overhead was not measured. S5-07
remains blocked/unaccepted.

